{"nodes": [{"id": "readme_bunkerflow_gateway", "label": "BunkerFlow Integration Gateway", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An event-driven integration gateway for bunker fuel trade data: ingests from business systems as scheduled batch pulls and real-time streams, normalizes onto one event contract, routes through Azure Service Bus, and lands in a lakehouse-style store. Deliberately sized to run on one machine."}, {"id": "readme_three_channels_one_pipeline", "label": "Three Ingestion Channels, One Pipeline", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Batch pull, Kafka stream and HTTP push all converge on a single IngestionPipeline. Adding a fourth source is an adapter plus a few field aliases, not a new code path."}, {"id": "readme_common_event_contract", "label": "Common Event Contract", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "IntegrationEvent is the single shape every channel produces. It is what makes a trade pulled from REST and one consumed from Kafka queryable identically in the lakehouse, distinguishable only by a channel column."}, {"id": "readme_normalization_aliases", "label": "Alias-Driven Field Mapping", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each source keeps its own field names; the normalizer maps aliases. Handles camelCase vs snake_case, comma decimals and mixed timestamp offsets so source systems are not forced to change."}, {"id": "readme_data_quality_checks", "label": "Data Quality Checks", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "IMO check-digit validation, UN/LOCODE format, known fuel grades, quantity and price ranges, future-dated trades."}, {"id": "readme_reserve_then_release", "label": "Reserve-Then-Release Deduplication", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The dedupe store claims the business key before publishing and gives it back if publishing fails. Marking a key as seen up front would make a retry of a failed publish look like a duplicate and lose the trade silently. Pinned by Should_release_the_business_key_when_publishing_never_succeeded."}, {"id": "readme_deterministic_event_id", "label": "Deterministic Event IDs", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Event id is a hash of source system plus source record id, so a replayed record produces the same id every time. That lets Service Bus duplicate detection reject a repeat before any consumer sees it, with the application dedupe store as the durable backstop."}, {"id": "readme_transient_vs_permanent", "label": "Transient vs Permanent Failure Types", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The retry policy only retries TransientPublishException. A missing topic or an oversized payload fails on the first attempt instead of spending the retry budget on something that cannot succeed."}, {"id": "readme_liveness_excludes_deps", "label": "Liveness Does Not Check Dependencies", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "/health/live reports only whether the process is up. Tying it to the database would make an orchestrator restart a healthy pod during a database blip. /health/ready is the probe that checks dependencies."}, {"id": "readme_validation_reports_all", "label": "Validation Reports Every Failure", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The validator returns all failures rather than the first, because a source system fixing one field at a time and resubmitting is a slow loop for everyone involved."}, {"id": "readme_offset_commit_rule", "label": "Kafka Offset Commit Rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A failed publish does not commit the offset: the consumer seeks back so the broker redelivers once infrastructure recovers. A rejected record is the opposite and IS committed, because resending bad data would only fail again; it goes to the dead-letter queue. Found while running the stack when the Service Bus emulator was still starting. Pinned by KafkaOffsetCommitTests against a real broker."}, {"id": "readme_loopback_mode", "label": "Loopback Mode", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "With no Service Bus connection string configured the gateway lands events in-process, so the whole system is demonstrable without Docker or any cloud account."}, {"id": "readme_split_credentials", "label": "Split Service Bus Credentials", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Separate send, listen and dead-letter credentials, none with Manage, so no component can do another component's job."}, {"id": "readme_dead_letter_paths", "label": "Two Dead-Letter Paths", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A dedicated queue for records rejected before publication, and the subscription's own DLQ for ones that fail after delivery. Failures before and after the broker are different problems and are kept apart."}, {"id": "readme_landing_dual_store", "label": "Dual Landing Store", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Postgres for querying and Parquet partitioned by trade date for the lakehouse. The same event lands in both."}, {"id": "readme_medallion_layers", "label": "Bronze / Silver / Gold Layers", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The Databricks notebook builds Delta tables over the gateway's Parquet: bronze as landed, silver with standardized column names and dedup on event id, gold aggregated by port and fuel grade."}, {"id": "readme_silver_dedup_noop", "label": "Silver Dedup Finding Nothing Is The Expected Result", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "50 bronze rows in, 50 silver rows out. The gateway already deduped on the business key before publishing, so the notebook finding nothing to drop is the two layers agreeing. It stays in because the landing writer flushes in batches and Service Bus is at-least-once, so a replayed file would otherwise double-count."}, {"id": "readme_rounding_parity", "label": "Half-Up Rounding Parity With Spark", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "scripts/sample-aggregates.sh rounds half-up to match Spark. C#'s default is banker's rounding, which disagrees on exact midpoints and made the two differ by 0.1 on one row before it was fixed."}, {"id": "readme_api_key_auth", "label": "Shared API Key Authentication", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "API key on the ingest and query endpoints, compared in constant time, with a key list so rotation does not break callers. Health and metrics stay open so probes and Prometheus can reach them. Honest limit: a shared key does not tell two source systems apart; OAuth or mTLS is the real answer."}, {"id": "readme_observability", "label": "Outcome And Channel Metrics", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Structured logs and Prometheus counters broken out by outcome (accepted, duplicate, rejected) and ingestion channel (batch, stream), so the dead-letter path is visible rather than theoretical."}, {"id": "readme_simulated_sources", "label": "Simulated Source Systems", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "/mock-sources/* generates trade data in two deliberately different shapes. There is no real ERP behind it. The ERP feed emits a broken IMO check digit every seventh record on purpose so the rejection path is exercised."}, {"id": "readme_scope_honesty", "label": "Honest Scope Boundaries", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The README states plainly what is simulated, what was applied once and destroyed, and what is a documented target only. Sources are simulated, Fabric is undeployed, Terraform was applied once to prove it, auth is a shared key, and there is no horizontal scaling, multi-region or schema registry."}], "edges": [{"source": "readme_three_channels_one_pipeline", "target": "src_bunkerflow_integration_pipeline_ingestionpipeline_bunkerflow_integration_pipeline_ingestionpipeline", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_three_channels_one_pipeline", "target": "src_bunkerflow_worker_ingestion_batchingestionworker_bunkerflow_worker_ingestion_batchingestionworker", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_three_channels_one_pipeline", "target": "src_bunkerflow_worker_ingestion_kafkaingestionworker_bunkerflow_worker_ingestion_kafkaingestionworker", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_common_event_contract", "target": "src_bunkerflow_contracts_integrationevent_bunkerflow_contracts_integrationevent", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_common_event_contract", "target": "src_bunkerflow_contracts_bunkertrade_bunkerflow_contracts_bunkertrade", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_normalization_aliases", "target": "src_bunkerflow_integration_normalization_bunkertradenormalizer_bunkerflow_integration_normalization_bunkertradenormalizer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_data_quality_checks", "target": "src_bunkerflow_integration_validation_bunkertradevalidator_bunkerflow_integration_validation_bunkertradevalidator", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_reserve_then_release", "target": "src_bunkerflow_integration_idempotency_postgresdeduplicationstore_bunkerflow_integration_idempotency_postgresdeduplicationstore", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_deterministic_event_id", "target": "src_bunkerflow_contracts_integrationevent_bunkerflow_contracts_integrationevent", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_deterministic_event_id", "target": "src_bunkerflow_integration_messaging_servicebuseventpublisher_bunkerflow_integration_messaging_servicebuseventpublisher", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_transient_vs_permanent", "target": "src_bunkerflow_integration_resilience_retrypolicy_bunkerflow_integration_resilience_retrypolicy", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_validation_reports_all", "target": "src_bunkerflow_integration_validation_bunkertradevalidator_bunkerflow_integration_validation_bunkertradevalidator", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "we